  {
    "id": "2046319023600931032",
    "created_at": "2026-04-20 16:04:08 -04:00",
    "full_text": "Having a stake cap through an issuance change also results in solo stakers being forced out. Large staking operations will be the last one standing due to economies of scale and defi demand.\n\nIf we keep issuance the same, this may become an issue in the future but we don't really know where the economic equalibrium lies. However, if we change the issuance curve then this outcome is guaranteed and will start immediately.\n\nThe only way I see how out of this endgame is by creating a native LST. I don't understand why there hasn't been research into this yet. This has been forseeable since LSTs have launched.",
