  {
    "id": "2046808618704462069",
    "created_at": "2026-04-22 00:29:37 -04:00",
    "full_text": "There is zero need to modify Ethereum's staking curve.  None.  Who decides that 1/3 of ETH staked is the right number?  I believe that it should be 2/3.  Why?  Because that is what a network capable of trillion dollar security will require.  It will need to be utterly unassailable.\n\nInstitutional stakers will stake regardless of the yield.  Solo stakers are largely priced out already with many moving to leveraged staking on Lido or Rocketpool to squeek out a few extra bps.\n\nThe question that needs answering is \"what is the percentage of ETH staked that is required to support the entire onchain economy in a manner that is bulletproof for 1000 years?\"\n\nNobody is asking that question.",
    "media": [],
    "screen_name": "_JohnWhelan",
