  {
    "id": "2046320850157109447",
    "created_at": "2026-04-20 16:11:24 -04:00",
    "full_text": "At a lower staking ratio you earn negative yield by pushing the limit to where yield reaches 0% and you still have time/monetary expenses in maintaining the validator\n\nEven if you assume that isn't the case, you're still pushing everyone out that doesn't have economies of scale\n\nAnd if you're assuming people are logical, at higher staking ratios you would assume people would stop staking once staking yield is 0, regardless of if it goes negative or not\n\nSo the difference in terms of 0 or negative is a red herring",
